# --- RaijinQuest: vendored world database (was pfQuest + pfQuest-ascension).
# Renamed and moved in-tree so a launcher update cannot overwrite it and so
# it can be extended. Order matters: base data, then locale, then the core
# addon, then the Ascension overrides that patch entries on top.
RaijinQuest\init\data.xml
RaijinQuest\init\enUS.xml
# addon.xml (the pfQuest UI: map, tracker, browser, journal, config) is
# DELIBERATELY NOT LOADED. We use RaijinQuest as a DATA SOURCE only. Its UI
# threw a cascade of errors when vendored, and this client is 32-bit: a
# crash dump showed 1.8GB of a 2GB address space in use with 140MB of Lua.
# QuestDB reads the tables directly and resolves names by inverting the
# locale tables itself, so none of that code is needed.
RaijinQuest\ascension\init\data-ascension.xml
RaijinQuest\ascension\init\enUS-ascension.xml
RaijinQuest\ascension\patchtable.lua
# RaijinQuest-ascension.lua is DELIBERATELY NOT LOADED: it is purely an
# update notifier for the upstream standalone addon - it polls a version over
# CHAT_MSG_ADDON, broadcasts to GUILD/PARTY/RAID, and prints a GitHub link.
# This copy is vendored so it can never update itself. Nothing references
# anything it defines (hcstrsplit, gpiupdater).
modules\questing\QuestDB.lua
modules\questing\QuestPolicy.lua
modules\questing\QuestInteract.lua
modules\questing\Escort.lua
modules\questing\Goals.lua
modules\questing\Suite.lua
modules\combat\Brain.lua
modules\gathering\Gatherer.lua
modules\grinding\Grinder.lua
